    {"id":"W27","kind":"step","q":"What is 74 − 46?","choices":["28","32","38","120"],"answer":"28","slips":{"32":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"Look at the ones place. You cannot take 6 from 4. You took the small digit from the big digit. Regroup first."},"38":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"You regrouped for the ones place. But you forgot to take 1 away from the tens place. The 7 there becomes 6."},"120":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"You added the two numbers. This problem needs you to subtract them."}},"explanation":"Yes. 74 − 46 = 28. Mia read 28 more pages.","pic":{"bar":{"total":74,"part":46}},"explain":{"bar":{"total":74,"part":46,"answer":28},"stack":{"a":74,"b":46,"op":"-"}}},
    {"id":"W28","q":"Town A has 682 people. Town B has 148 people. How many more people live in Town A than in Town B?","choices":["534","544","546","830"],"answer":"534","hint":"\"How many more\" means subtract. Put the big number first.","pic":{"bar":{"total":682,"part":148}},"slips":{"544":{"tag":"Forgot to take 1 after regrouping","say":"You regrouped for the ones place. But you forgot to take 1 away from the tens place. The 8 there becomes 7."},"546":{"tag":"Took the small digit from the big digit","say":"Look at the ones place. You cannot take 8 from 2. You took the small digit from the big digit. Regroup first."},"830":{"tag":"Added instead of subtracting","say":"You added the two numbers. This problem needs you to subtract them."}},"explanation":"\"How many more\" means subtract. Take the small number from the big number. 682 − 148 = 534.","explain":{"bar":{"total":682,"part":148,"answer":534},"stack":{"a":682,"b":148,"op":"-"}}},
    {"id":"W29","q":"Leo read 721 pages. Kim read 387 pages. How many fewer pages did Kim read than Leo?","choices":["334","344","466","1,108"],"answer":"334","hint":"\"How many fewer\" means subtract too. Put the big number first.","pic":{"bar":{"total":721,"part":387}},"slips":{"344":{"tag":"Forgot to take 1 after regrouping","say":"You regrouped for the ones place. But you forgot to take 1 away from the tens place. The 2 there becomes 1."},"466":{"tag":"Took the small digit from the big digit","say":"Look at the ones place. You cannot take 7 from 1. You took the small digit from the big digit. Regroup first. Regroup in the tens place too."},"1,108":{"tag":"Added instead of subtracting","say":"You added the two numbers. This problem needs you to subtract them."}},"explanation":"\"How many fewer\" means subtract. Take the small number from the big number. 721 − 387 = 334.","explain":{"bar":{"total":721,"part":387,"answer":334},"stack":{"a":721,"b":387,"op":"-"}}},
    {"id":"W30","kind":"watch","title":"Rounding to the nearest thousand","text":"Round 3,700 to the nearest thousand.\n3,700 is between 3,000 and 4,000.\nLook at the hundreds digit. It is 7. 5 or more rounds up. 4 or less rounds down.\n7 is 5 or more. So 3,700 rounds up to 4,000.","pic":{"work":["3,000  ←  3,700  →  4,000"]}},
    {"id":"W31","kind":"step","q":"Round 6,420 to the nearest thousand. 6,420 is between which two thousands?","choices":["6,000 and 7,000","6,400 and 6,500","5,000 and 6,000"],"answer":"6,000 and 7,000","slips":{"6,400 and 6,500":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"Those are hundreds. The nearest thousand is 6,000 or 7,000."},"5,000 and 6,000":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"6,420 is more than 6,000. It is between 6,000 and 7,000."}},"explanation":"Yes. 6,420 is between 6,000 and 7,000.","explain":{"work":["6,000  ←  6,420  →  7,000"]}},
    {"id":"W32","kind":"step","q":"Which digit tells you which way to round?","choices":["The hundreds digit, 4","The tens digit, 2","The thousands digit, 6"],"answer":"The hundreds digit, 4","slips":{"The tens digit, 2":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"For the nearest thousand, look at the hundreds digit. In 6,420 it is 4."},"The thousands digit, 6":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"For the nearest thousand, look at the hundreds digit. In 6,420 it is 4."}},"explanation":"Yes. The hundreds digit is 4.","pic":{"work":["6,000  ←  6,420  →  7,000"]}},
    {"id":"W33","kind":"step","q":"The hundreds digit is 4. So 6,420 rounds to what?","choices":["6,000","7,000","6,400"],"answer":"6,000","slips":{"7,000":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"4 is 4 or less. Round down to 6,000."},"6,400":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"6,400 is the nearest hundred. This asks for the nearest thousand."}},"explanation":"Yes. 4 is 4 or less, so round down. 6,420 rounds to 6,000.","pic":{"work":["6,000  ←  6,420  →  7,000"]},"explain":{"work":["6,420 → 6,000"]}},
    {"id":"W34","q":"Round 1,590 to the nearest thousand.","choices":["1,000","1,590","1,600","2,000"],"answer":"2,000","hint":"Look at the hundreds digit. 5 or more rounds up. 4 or less rounds down.","pic":{"work":["1,000  ←  1,590  →  2,000"]},"slips":{"1,000":{"tag":"Rounded the wrong way","say":"Look at the hundreds place in 1,590. It is 5. 5 or more rounds up."},"1,600":{"tag":"Rounded to the wrong place","say":"You rounded to the nearest hundred. This one says nearest thousand. Look at the hundreds place."},"1,590":{"tag":"Rounded to the wrong place","say":"You rounded to the nearest ten. This one says nearest thousand. Look at the hundreds place."}},"explanation":"1,590 is between 1,000 and 2,000. The hundreds digit is 5. That is 5 or more, so round up. 1,590 rounds to 2,000.","explain":{"work":["1,590 → 2,000"]}},
    {"id":"W35","kind":"watch","title":"Estimating","text":"To estimate, round each number first. Then add. 3,800 + 2,100.\n3,800 rounds to 4,000. 2,100 rounds to 2,000.\n4,000 + 2,000 = 6,000. The estimate is 6,000.","pic":{"work":["3,800 → 4,000","2,100 → 2,000","4,000 + 2,000 = 6,000"]}},
    {"id":"W36","q":"Round each number to the nearest thousand. Then add. 4,800 + 7,700","choices":["12,000","13,000","14,000","15,000"],"answer":"13,000","hint":"Round each number first. Then add the two rounded numbers.","pic":{"work":["4,800 → ?","7,700 → ?"]},"slips":{"12,000":{"tag":"Rounded the wrong way","say":"4,800 rounds up to 5,000. Look at the hundreds place. It is 8. 5 or more rounds up."},"14,000":{"tag":"Rounded the wrong way","say":"Check your rounding. Look at the hundreds place. 4,800 rounds to 5,000. 7,700 rounds to 8,000."},"15,000":{"tag":"Rounded the wrong way","say":"Check your rounding. Look at the hundreds place. 4,800 rounds to 5,000. 7,700 rounds to 8,000."}},"explanation":"Round first. 4,800 rounds to 5,000. 7,700 rounds to 8,000. Then add. 5,000 + 8,000 = 13,000.","explain":{"work":["4,800 → 5,000","7,700 → 8,000","5,000 + 8,000 = 13,000"]}},
    {"id":"W37","kind":"watch","title":"Perimeter","text":"Perimeter is the distance around a shape. Add all four sides.\nThis rectangle is 6 feet long and 3 feet wide. The sides across from each other are the same.\n6 + 3 + 6 + 3 = 18. The perimeter is 18 feet.","pic":{"rect":{"l":6,"w":3,"unit":"ft","sides":"all"}}},
    {"id":"W38","kind":"step","q":"This rectangle is 5 meters long and 2 meters wide. How many sides does it have?","choices":["4","2","3"],"answer":"4","slips":{"2":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"Count again. A rectangle has 4 sides. Two numbers show, but there are 4 sides."},"3":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"Count again. A rectangle has 4 sides."}},"explanation":"Yes. A rectangle has 4 sides.","pic":{"rect":{"l":5,"w":2,"unit":"m","sides":"two"}},"explain":{"rect":{"l":5,"w":2,"unit":"m","sides":"all"}}},
    {"id":"W39","kind":"step","q":"Which numbers do you add to find the perimeter?","choices":["5 + 2 + 5 + 2","5 + 2","5 × 2"],"answer":"5 + 2 + 5 + 2","slips":{"5 + 2":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"You added only two sides: 5 + 2. A rectangle has four sides. Add 5 and 2 one more time."},"5 × 2":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"You multiplied 5 × 2. That is not the perimeter. Perimeter means add the four sides."}},"explanation":"Yes. Add all four sides: 5 + 2 + 5 + 2.","pic":{"rect":{"l":5,"w":2,"unit":"m","sides":"all"}}},
    {"id":"W40","kind":"step","q":"What is 5 + 2 + 5 + 2?","choices":["14 meters","7 meters","10 meters"],"answer":"14 meters","slips":{"7 meters":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"You added only two sides: 5 + 2. A rectangle has four sides. Add 5 and 2 one more time."},"10 meters":{"tag":"Warm-Up step","say":"You multiplied 5 × 2. That is not the perimeter. Perimeter means add the four sides."}},"explanation":"Yes. 5 + 2 + 5 + 2 = 14. The perimeter is 14 meters.","pic":{"rect":{"l":5,"w":2,"unit":"m","sides":"all"}}},
    {"id":"W41","q":"A rectangle is 8 feet long and 2 feet wide. What is the perimeter?","choices":["10 feet","16 feet","18 feet","20 feet"],"answer":"20 feet","hint":"Two sides are not labeled. The sides across from each other match. Add all four sides.","pic":{"rect":{"l":8,"w":2,"unit":"ft","sides":"two"}},"slips":{"10 feet":{"tag":"Added only some of the sides","say":"You added only two sides: 8 + 2. A rectangle has four sides. Add 8 and 2 one more time."},"18 feet":{"tag":"Added only some of the sides","say":"You added only three sides: 8 + 8 + 2. One side is missing. Add one more 2."},"16 feet":{"tag":"Found area instead of perimeter","say":"You multiplied 8 × 2. That is not the perimeter. Perimeter means add the four sides."}},"explanation":"Perimeter is the distance around. Add all four sides. 8 + 8 + 2 + 2 = 20 feet.","explain":{"rect":{"l":8,"w":2,"unit":"ft","sides":"all"}}},
    {"id":"W42","q":"Each side of a square is 10 inches. What is the perimeter?","choices":["20 inches","30 inches","40 inches","100 inches"],"answer":"40 inches","hint":"A square has four sides that are all the same. Add all four.","pic":{"rect":{"l":10,"w":10,"unit":"in.","sides":"one"}},"slips":{"20 inches":{"tag":"Added only some of the sides","say":"You added only two sides: 10 + 10. A square has four sides. Add all four."},"30 inches":{"tag":"Added only some of the sides","say":"You added only three sides: 10 + 10 + 10. A square has four sides. Add one more 10."},"100 inches":{"tag":"Found area instead of perimeter","say":"You multiplied 10 × 10. That is not the perimeter. Perimeter means add the four sides."}},"explanation":"A square has four equal sides. Add all four sides. 10 + 10 + 10 + 10 = 40 inches.","explain":{"rect":{"l":10,"w":10,"unit":"in.","sides":"all"}}}
